1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,853
Business Case 12 begins when the worker starts or an effective
relationship change is proposed.

2
00:00:07,853 --> 00:00:12,565
Milestones and transition effects remain effective-dated, reversible and
reconciled.

3
00:00:12,565 --> 00:00:15,182
The governed record is TRN-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:21,465
The accountable actors are Employee, Manager, Buddy, People Operations,
HRIS, IT, Facilities.

5
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:29,318
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:29,318 --> 00:00:35,121
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 5 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:35,121 --> 00:00:45,568
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:45,568 --> 00:00:51,371
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:51,371 --> 00:00:54,843
Process 1, Employee: Complete day-one and 30/60/90 milestones.

10
00:00:54,843 --> 00:01:00,918
The action record progress and support needs produces milestone evidence
in the Journey ledger.

11
00:01:00,918 --> 00:01:03,956
Process 2, People Operations: Propose effective-dated transition.

12
00:01:03,956 --> 00:01:09,597
The action select transition and reason produces transition draft in the
Lifecycle ledger.

13
00:01:09,597 --> 00:01:12,635
Process 3, Approvers: Preview impact and approve.

14
00:01:12,635 --> 00:01:18,710
The action compare before and after produces approved execution plan in
the Lifecycle ledger.

15
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:21,748
Process 4, System Owners: Execute or compensate.

16
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:27,823
The action create downstream work produces per-destination effects and
receipts in the Effect ledger.

17
00:01:27,823 --> 00:01:30,861
Process 5, People Operations: Reconcile final state.

18
00:01:30,861 --> 00:01:37,804
The action compare expected and observed produces closed, blocked or
restated outcome in the Analytics store.

19
00:01:37,804 --> 00:01:40,227
The actual product route is /hr/transitions/TRN-DEMO-001/impact.

20
00:01:40,227 --> 00:01:45,880
It presents worker-transition execution and compensating-work graph in
the surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

21
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:55,974
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

22
00:01:55,974 --> 00:01:58,910
The seeded workbench follows record TRN-DEMO-001.

23
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:17,997
Its governed fields are Transition, Crossboard to Product Design;
Effective date, December 1, 2026; Before, Recruiting Ops , SF; After,
Product Design , Remote CA; Downstream effects, HRIS, IGA, benefits,
facilities; Partial state, HRIS success , 3 effects pending.

24
00:02:17,997 --> 00:02:27,296
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

25
00:02:27,296 --> 00:02:30,610
With People Operations selected, we perform approve and execute
transition.

26
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:34,919
The guard requires impact owners, approvals, effective date and safe
execution order pass.

27
00:02:34,919 --> 00:02:45,194
The state changes from Impact preview to Reconciled with compensation,
records WorkerTransitionReconciled, writes to the Lifecycle effect
ledger, and creates the handoff: HRIS, IT, facilities and benefits
owners receive ordered work.

28
00:02:45,194 --> 00:02:49,722
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate partial downstream
success.

29
00:02:49,722 --> 00:02:54,702
The prepared failure is HRIS succeeded but access and benefits failed.

30
00:02:54,702 --> 00:03:04,210
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

31
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:07,007
The owned recovery is Run compensating work.

32
00:03:07,007 --> 00:03:11,003
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

33
00:03:11,003 --> 00:03:16,198
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

34
00:03:16,198 --> 00:03:25,389
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through transition completion, partial failures and compensation age and
minimum-context next-actor work.

35
00:03:25,389 --> 00:03:27,797
Business Case 12 is complete.

36
00:03:27,797 --> 00:03:41,763
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

37
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:46,098
Milestones and transition effects remain effective-dated, reversible and
reconciled.

38
00:03:46,098 --> 00:03:51,395
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
